      "unit": "mm"
     }
    }
   },
   "date": {
    "after": "1909-12-16",
    "@annotation": {
     "@id": "premises#advance-half-mm-annotation",
     "belief": {
      "@type": "belief",
      "@id": "premises#advance-half-mm-belief",
      "certainty": "likely",
      "reasons": [
       {
        "@type": "inference",
        "premises": [],
        "used": [
         "https://w3id.org/welte-premises/evidence/advance",
         "https://github.com/pfefferniels/condon-dates/blob/f6ec84ec54d2a4d2ff50c2898cebea36b6a66516/data/readings.json",
         "https://github.com/pfefferniels/condon-dates/blob/f6ec84ec54d2a4d2ff50c2898cebea36b6a66516/data/perforator.json",
         "https://github.com/pfefferniels/condon-dates/blob/f6ec84ec54d2a4d2ff50c2898cebea36b6a66516/premises.py",
         "https://github.com/pfefferniels/welte225.org/blob/0f6bcfb85154f3d2c2928049b7518463fad1d1c9/punch-225/dates/step.py"
        ],
        "note": "The advance resolves, at a strength of at least 0.25, at 0.85 to 1.15 mm on 11 copies dated to the day at high or medium confidence, from 1908-11-20 to 1909-12-16, and under 0.75 mm on 191, from 1910-05-21 to 1928-06-19; no dated copy falls on the wrong side. The perforator was still at the early advance on the day of the last early copy, Welte 569 of 1909-12-16 (https://purl.stanford.edu/rb625rv7300), and the bound rests on that copy's date alone. The rolls before it that do not resolve are not late-advance rolls hiding: a comb at 0.5 mm is the easier of the two to see (punch-225/dates/README.md)."
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "premises#paper-red-cool",
   "company": {
    "name": "M. Welte & Söhne",
    "sameAs": [
     "https://d-nb.info/gnd/5125268-5"
    ]
   },
   "system": {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/reo/type/system/welte-t100"
   },
   "paper": {
    "@id": "papers#red-cool",
    "name": "cool red paper"
   },
   "date": {
    "after": "1911-08-24",
    "@annotation": {
     "@id": "premises#paper-red-cool-annotation",
     "belief": {
      "@type": "belief",
      "@id": "premises#paper-red-cool-belief",
      "certainty": "likely",
      "reasons": [
       {
        "@type": "inference",
        "premises": [],
        "used": [
         "https://w3id.org/welte-premises/evidence/paper",
         "https://w3id.org/welte-premises/papers",
         "https://github.com/pfefferniels/condon-dates/blob/f6ec84ec54d2a4d2ff50c2898cebea36b6a66516/paper/colour.json",
         "https://github.com/pfefferniels/condon-dates/blob/f6ec84ec54d2a4d2ff50c2898cebea36b6a66516/paper/colour.py",
         "https://github.com/pfefferniels/condon-dates/blob/f6ec84ec54d2a4d2ff50c2898cebea36b6a66516/data/readings.json",
         "https://github.com/pfefferniels/condon-dates/blob/f6ec84ec54d2a4d2ff50c2898cebea36b6a66516/data/perforator.json",
         "https://github.com/pfefferniels/condon-dates/blob/f6ec84ec54d2a4d2ff50c2898cebea36b6a66516/premises.py"
        ],
        "note": "148 rolls measure as cool red paper (a* at least 10 and b* under 15, corrected CIELAB), 112 of them dated to the day at high or medium confidence, from 1911-08-24 to 1928-06-19. All 148 whose chain pitch is measured were punched on the narrow perforator. The bound rests on the first dated copy, Welte 1697 of 1911-08-24 (https://purl.stanford.edu/vf252dc4872), alone; the 56 dated copies before it are all of other paper."
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "@id": "premises#paper-red-warm-bright",
   "company": {
    "name": "M. Welte & Söhne",
    "sameAs": [
     "https://d-nb.info/gnd/5125268-5"
    ]
   },
   "system": {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/reo/type/system/welte-t100"
   },
   "paper": {
    "@id": "papers#red-warm-bright",
    "name": "bright warm red paper"
   },
   "date": {
    "after": "1923-11-08",
    "before": "1925-11-21",
    "@annotation": {
     "@id": "premises#paper-red-warm-bright-annotation",
     "belief": {
      "@type": "belief",
      "@id": "premises#paper-red-warm-bright-belief",
      "certainty": "likely",
      "reasons": [
       {
        "@type": "inference",
        "premises": [],
        "used": [
         "https://w3id.org/welte-premises/evidence/paper",
         "https://w3id.org/welte-premises/papers",
         "https://github.com/pfefferniels/condon-dates/blob/f6ec84ec54d2a4d2ff50c2898cebea36b6a66516/paper/colour.json",
         "https://github.com/pfefferniels/condon-dates/blob/f6ec84ec54d2a4d2ff50c2898cebea36b6a66516/paper/colour.py",
         "https://github.com/pfefferniels/condon-dates/blob/f6ec84ec54d2a4d2ff50c2898cebea36b6a66516/data/readings.json",
         "https://github.com/pfefferniels/condon-dates/blob/f6ec84ec54d2a4d2ff50c2898cebea36b6a66516/data/perforator.json",
         "https://github.com/pfefferniels/condon-dates/blob/f6ec84ec54d2a4d2ff50c2898cebea36b6a66516/premises.py"
        ],
        "note": "24 rolls measure as bright warm red paper (warm red with a* at least 32, corrected CIELAB), 16 of them dated to the day at high or medium confidence, from 1923-11-08 to 1925-11-21. All 24 whose chain pitch is measured were punched on the narrow perforator. The bounds rest on the first and the last dated copy, Welte 1213 of 1923-11-08 (https://purl.stanford.edu/vj076nk8220) and Welte 5661 of 1925-11-21 (https://purl.stanford.edu/cw965qx3168). Its dates lie closer together than chance allows: 1.4 years between the tenth and the ninetieth percentile, against 14.6 years for random groups of as many dated copies of warm red paper, of which 0 in 10000 were as close. Within a unit of the rule's edge lie 2 dated copies; that of 1922-05-14 lies outside the window and would widen it under a looser rule."
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   }
  },
